1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,035
The screen promised ten thousand dollars by midnight would make Mara perfect forever.

2
00:00:06,235 --> 00:00:12,175
One buyer offered ten thousand dollars. In exchange, they would own every ending the theatre ever made.

3
00:00:13,375 --> 00:00:18,010
June found the catch. The payment was only authorized. No money had arrived.

4
00:00:19,210 --> 00:00:24,770
The theatre sold honest tickets to its real show. Ninety nine seats were taken. One remained.

5
00:00:25,977 --> 00:00:30,392
A stranger came for a play, not a miracle. She bought the final seat.

6
00:00:31,592 --> 00:00:39,207
One hundred paid tickets at one hundred dollars made ten thousand dollars in story sales. Costs and refunds still matter.

7
00:00:40,407 --> 00:00:46,812
The Presenter painted a halo on Mara. She stepped aside. The money was real. The promise was not proven.

8
00:00:48,012 --> 00:00:53,452
The projector went dark. Someone coughed. The house bell rang. Mara said, I am here.
